    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to match the spec.\n\n**New `Soundex` helper** (`.../rest/controller/v1/Soundex.java`): a self-contained standard American Soundex encoder (matching the style of the existing hand-rolled `Sha256`/`HouseholdNormalizer` helpers), producing the four-character phonetic code for a last name.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n- `buildIdentityKey` now returns `Sha256.hex(normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName))` \u2014 a 64-char hex digest instead of the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`.\n- Renamed `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` \u2192 `rejectDuplicateIdentity`: the 409 now fires on an `identityKey` collision against **any** non-deleted owner (the single identity key is the whole of duplicate detection), rather than the old household-scoped check. The separate household-id 409 block is gone. Soft-deleted owners are still ignored, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeEmail`, before identity is resolved).\n- `findPossibleDuplicate` (soft match) now triggers when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match \u2014 so two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are created as a soft match instead of being rejected.\n- `householdId` is still derived (it drives household size and the membership-level cap), just no longer part of the identity key or a rejection trigger.\n\n**Docs:** updated the relevant javadoc and the `identityKey` schema description/example in `openapi.yml`.\n\nTest suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (409 on identical identity) both green.",
